  <h1>grant-crypto SDK — {{ goat_get_sdk_release_tag }}</h1>
  <p>A small cross-language library for encrypting data so that only the
     intended members can read it. Encryption and decryption happen entirely
     inside your process — the platform distributes wrapped keys but never holds
     one that can read your data, and rotating your key destroys the old one so
     past traffic stays unreadable. One audited core (Rust) sits behind a C ABI;
     thin Go, Python, and TypeScript wrappers call the same core.</p>

  <p style="margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.9rem 1.1rem;border:1px solid #3a2f1f;border-left:3px solid #e8b04b;border-radius:6px;background:#211b13;">
    <strong style="color:#e8b04b;">&#128214; Documentation</strong> &mdash;
    the full, rich <a href="docs/">grant-crypto SDK documentation site</a>
    (concepts, quickstart in all four languages, API + C-ABI reference, wire
    format, security, troubleshooting). Served here from the same pinned
    release; the same pages ship inside the SDK source tarball at
    <code>sdk/docs/site/</code>.
  </p>

{# Split the served assets into the source tarball and the prebuilt C ABI
   libraries. Drop the *.sha256 sidecars + the aggregate SHA256SUMS from the
   primary lists (they're checksum text, surfaced per-artifact and in the
   disclosure). The docs tarball is unpacked into docs/ (linked above), not
