{%   elif a.startswith('grant-crypto-sdk-docs-') %}
{#      docs tarball — unpacked into docs/, surfaced via the link above #}
{%   else %}
{%     set _ = src_tarballs.append(a) %}
{%   endif %}
{% endfor %}

  <h2>Prebuilt C ABI libraries</h2>
  <p>The audited FFI seam (a shared library + static library + the C header) that
     the Go/Python/TS bindings link against. Grab the one for your platform —
     you only need the source tarball below if you want to build the core
     yourself. Each carries a sibling <code>.sha256</code>; verify before use.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Artifact</th><th>Verify</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
{% for a in capi_tarballs %}
{%   set core = a[('grant-crypto-capi-' | length):] | replace('.tar.gz', '') %}
{%   set os = core.split('-')[0] %}
{%   set arch = core.split('-')[1] %}
{%   set os_name = {'darwin': 'macOS', 'linux': 'Linux'}[os] %}
{%   set arch_name = ({'arm64': 'Apple Silicon', 'amd64': 'Intel'}[arch] if os == 'darwin' else {'arm64': 'arm64', 'amd64': 'x86-64'}[arch]) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ os_name }} · {{ arch_name }}</td>
        <td><a href="{{ a }}">{{ a }}</a></td>
        <td><a href="{{ a }}.sha256">.sha256</a></td>
      </tr>
{% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Fetch + verify a prebuilt library</h3>
  <pre>lib=grant-crypto-capi-linux-amd64.tar.gz   # pick your platform from the table
curl -fsSL https://{{ goat_get_hostname }}/{{ goat_get_sdk_www_subdir }}/$lib       -o "$lib"
curl -fsSL https://{{ goat_get_hostname }}/{{ goat_get_sdk_www_subdir }}/$lib.sha256 -o "$lib.sha256"
sha256sum -c "$lib.sha256"        # macOS: shasum -a 256 -c "$lib.sha256"
tar xzf "$lib"                    # -> the .so/.dylib, libgrant_crypto_capi.a, include/, INSTALL.txt</pre>

  <h2>Source tarball — build from source</h2>
  <p>The complete SDK workspace (Rust core + C ABI + all bindings) plus the
     shared conformance vectors and the wire-format spec, re-rooted so it builds
     standalone. Use this to build the C ABI library on an unlisted platform or
     to run the test suite.</p>
{% for a in src_tarballs %}
  <p class="files"><a href="{{ a }}">{{ a }}</a>
     <a href="{{ a }}.sha256">.sha256</a></p>
  <pre>curl -fsSL https://{{ goat_get_hostname }}/{{ goat_get_sdk_www_subdir }}/{{ a }}        -o {{ a }}
curl -fsSL https://{{ goat_get_hostname }}/{{ goat_get_sdk_www_subdir }}/{{ a }}.sha256 -o {{ a }}.sha256
sha256sum -c {{ a }}.sha256        # macOS: shasum -a 256 -c {{ a }}.sha256
tar xzf {{ a }}
cd grant-crypto/sdk
cargo build -p grant-crypto-capi   # builds the shared + static library under target/
cargo test                          # optional: runs the conformance + roundtrip suites</pre>
{% endfor %}

  <h2>Language setup</h2>
  <p>Each binding's own <code>README.md</code> in the source tarball
     (<code>grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/&lt;lang&gt;/</code>) is the authoritative,
     CI-tested quickstart; the essentials:</p>

  <h3>Rust (the core crate directly)</h3>
  <pre>cd grant-crypto/sdk
cargo add --path core          # or depend on ./core from your workspace
# use grant_crypto::datapath::{acquire_stream_key, Context, KeyStore};</pre>

  <h3>Go</h3>
  <pre># from your module, point at the unpacked binding + link the static library:
go mod edit -replace github.com/usareur-af/goatcore/ops/grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/go=./grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/go
# the cgo directives link libgrant_crypto_capi.a — build it (source tarball) or
# use the prebuilt one, then set the LDFLAGS search path per the binding README.
CGO_ENABLED=1 go build ./...</pre>
  <p><small>Go ≥ 1.22. The binding is <code>import gc
     "github.com/usareur-af/goatcore/ops/grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/go"</code>,
     zero Go dependencies, cgo over the static library.</small></p>

  <h3>Python</h3>
  <pre>pip install ./grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/python     # stdlib ctypes; zero pip deps
export GRANT_CRYPTO_CAPI_LIB=/path/to/capi/dir     # dir holding the .so/.dylib
python -c "import grant_crypto as gc; print(gc.__name__)"</pre>
  <p><small>Python ≥ 3.8. Import name is <code>grant_crypto</code>. Point
     <code>GRANT_CRYPTO_CAPI_LIB</code> at the directory (or file) of the shared
     library from the prebuilt tarball or your <code>cargo build</code>.</small></p>

  <h3>TypeScript / Node</h3>
  <pre>cd grant-crypto/sdk/bindings/ts
npm install && npm run build                        # tsc -> dist/
export GRANT_CRYPTO_CAPI_LIB=/path/to/lib.{so,dylib}
npm test                                            # runs the conformance suite</pre>
  <p><small>Node ≥ 20. Package name is <code>grant-crypto</code>; koffi loads the
     shared library at runtime from <code>GRANT_CRYPTO_CAPI_LIB</code> (or a
     relative dev path). Consume it from your project via the built package or
     <code>npm link</code>.</small></p>

